tasks.details:
In .github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml, change the deploy-backend job step:
  --image ${{ env.BACKEND_IMAGE }}:staging-${{ github.sha }}
to:
  --image ${{ env.BACKEND_IMAGE }}:${{ needs.build-backend.outputs.image_tag }}
Also add build-backend to the needs list of deploy-backend job so the output is accessible.

## Context

- Frontend: deployed to Vercel on every push to main via `.github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml`
- Backend: deployed to Hetzner VPS via SSH + Docker Compose (container: `modishlog-backend`, port 8000)
- DB: Neon cloud PostgreSQL (unchanged — no work needed here)
- Production nginx config lives at `nginx/nginx.prod.conf` on the Hetzner VPS (served inside a Docker container)
- Relevant GitHub Secrets: `STAGING_DATABASE_URL`, `STAGING_SECRET_KEY`, `STAGING_CORS_ORIGINS`, `STAGING_API_URL`, `VERCEL_TOKEN`, `VERCEL_ORG_ID`, `VERCEL_PROJECT_ID`, `HETZNER_HOST`, `HETZNER_SSH_KEY`

---

## Step 1 — DNS records (done manually in your DNS registrar, NOT in code)

Add two records under modishlog.com:

| Type  | Name                      | Value                        |
|-------|---------------------------|------------------------------|
| CNAME | staging.modishlog.com     | cname.vercel-dns.com         |
| A     | api.staging.modishlog.com | &lt;Hetzner VPS public IP&gt;      |

DNS TTL: 300s (5 min) so changes propagate quickly.

---

## Step 2 — Vercel custom domain (done manually in Vercel dashboard)

1. Go to Vercel dashboard → modishlog project → Settings → Domains
2. Add `staging.modishlog.com`
3. Vercel will verify the CNAME and auto-provision a Let's Encrypt SSL cert
4. Remove or demote the old auto-generated Vercel URL if desired

---

## Step 3 — Nginx config on Hetzner (`nginx/nginx.prod.conf`)

Add a new server block for the staging API alongside the existing production block. The staging backend container is named `modishlog-backend` and listens on port 8000 inside the Docker network.

```nginx
# ── HTTP → HTTPS redirect for staging API ─────────────────────────────────
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name api.staging.modishlog.com;

    location /.well-known/acme-challenge/ {
        root /var/www/certbot;
    }

    location / {
        return 301 https://api.staging.modishlog.com$request_uri;
    }
}

# ── Staging API server ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    server_name api.staging.modishlog.com;

    ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/api.staging.modishlog.com/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/api.staging.modishlog.com/privkey.pem;
    include /etc/nginx/snippets/ssl-params.conf;

    add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains" always;
    add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff" always;

    location /health {
        proxy_pass http://modishlog-backend:8000;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        access_log off;
    }

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://modishlog-backend:8000;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_read_timeout 60s;
        proxy_connect_timeout 10s;
    }
}
```

After updating the file, copy it to the Hetzner VPS and reload nginx:
```bash
scp nginx/nginx.prod.conf root@<HETZNER_HOST>:/root/modishlog-prod/nginx/nginx.prod.conf
ssh root@<HETZNER_HOST> "docker exec <nginx-container> nginx -t && docker exec <nginx-container> nginx -s reload"
```

---

## Step 4 — SSL certificate on Hetzner (done manually via SSH)

SSH into Hetzner and run certbot for the new subdomain:
```bash
docker exec <certbot-container> certbot --nginx -d api.staging.modishlog.com --non-interactive --agree-tos -m admin@modishlog.com
```

Or if certbot runs as a standalone service:
```bash
certbot certonly --webroot -w /var/www/certbot -d api.staging.modishlog.com
```

Verify the cert exists at `/etc/letsencrypt/live/api.staging.modishlog.com/`.

---

## Step 5 — Update GitHub Secrets (done manually in GitHub → Settings → Secrets)

| Secret               | New value                                          |
|----------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| `STAGING_API_URL`    | `https://api.staging.modishlog.com`                |
| `STAGING_CORS_ORIGINS` | `https://staging.modishlog.com` (replace old Vercel URL) |

---

## Step 6 — Code changes (committed to repo)

### `docker-compose.staging.yml`
Update the CORS_ORIGINS comment and default to reflect the new domain:
```yaml
CORS_ORIGINS: ${STAGING_CORS_ORIGINS:-https://staging.modishlog.com}
```

### `frontend/vercel.json` (create if it does not exist, or update)
Ensure the build uses the `STAGING_API_URL` env var and the domain alias is declared:
```json
{
  "alias": ["staging.modishlog.com"],
  "buildCommand": "ng build --configuration production",
  "outputDirectory": "dist/frontend/browser"
}
```

### `.github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml`
Add a smoke-test step after deployment to verify both URLs respond:
```yaml
- name: Smoke test staging
  run: |
    curl -sf https://staging.modishlog.com | grep -q "ModishLog" || exit 1
    curl -sf https://api.staging.modishlog.com/health | grep -q "ok" || exit 1
```

---

## Step 7 — Verify end-to-end

1. Open https://staging.modishlog.com — should load the Angular app with valid SSL
2. Open https://api.staging.modishlog.com/health — should return `{"status":"ok"}`
3. Log in on staging — should authenticate against the Neon DB without CORS errors
4. Check browser DevTools Network tab — API calls should go to `api.staging.modishlog.com`, not an IP

---

## What NOT to change
- Production nginx blocks (`modishlog.com`, `www.modishlog.com`) — leave untouched
- Production DB or backend container — leave untouched
- Any backend application code — this is purely infrastructure/config
